plaso.tsv: what plaso (the log2timeline/plaso:20260720 Docker image) reads
from the samples in tests/fixtures/plaso/ with its jsonl parser
(aws_cloudtrail_log, azure_activity_log, gcp_log, microsoft365_audit_log
plugins; psort -o json_line), one line per event: the file, the time
(microseconds since 1970, UTC), then the values compared, by plugin:

- CloudTrail: event name, source, user name, user ARN, source address,
  resources, access key;
- Microsoft 365: operation, workload, user id, user key, client address,
  object id, result, record id, record type, user type, organisation;
- Azure activity: operation, resource provider, caller, client address,
  resource id, event data id, level, correlation id, resource group,
  resource type, subscription, tenant, event name;
- Google Cloud: method, service, principal e-mail, actor user, caller
  address, user agent, resource name, status message, log name, severity,
  text payload, event subtype.

Lists are joined with ", ". Written from plaso's output, not from this
crate.

written.tsv: the main fields of the records in tests/fixtures/written/
(formats plaso has no samples of), as Python's own JSON and CSV modules
read them, written by gen.py (see its header).
